---
id: boiled-rice-stick-noodles
title: Boiled Rice Stick Noodles
category: modular_carb

yield:
  servings: 1
  cooked_g: 140

storage:
  fridge_days: 4
  freezer_friendly: false

equipment:
  - saucepan
---

In a #saucepan, bring 1000 ml of water to a rolling boil over high heat.

Submerge @rice-stick-noodles{63%g} into the boiling water. Stir gently with tongs or chopsticks to separate strands so they do not stick together. Boil undisturbed for ~boil-time{4.5%min} until tender with a slight chew (al dente).

Drain immediately in a colander and rinse thoroughly under cold running water for ~rinse-time{30%sec} to wash off excess surface starches and halt carryover cooking, preventing gummy clumping.

Shake off excess water thoroughly. Transfer the cooked noodles (140 g cooked yield) into a meal prep container and let cool before sealing.
